# A small game's shapes compile without unhandled ops: const tables read by
# index, register writes through volatile pointers in loops, and a table
# lookup at a computed index (ported from opensnes-emu
# test_animation_patterns, which rejected unhandled ops and assembled it).
absent ; unhandled op
# Const tables live in the asset banks: C reads them with the indexed
# long form, whose bank comes from the symbol (#121, #127.3).
in load_tiles: present tax\n\tsep #\$20\n\tlda\.l tile_data,x\n
in load_palette: present tax\n\tlda\.l palette,x\n
in get_tile_for_state: present tax\n\tsep #\$20\n\tlda\.l frame_tiles,x\n
# Each branch writes its port through the pointer: 8-bit store via X,
# within the branch (the match may not cross a jmp or a label).
# Re-pinned 2026-10-08: a store through a pointer loads X first, then the
# value (`tax` / `lda` / `sta.l $00NNNN,x`); no pha / pla around it.
in load_tiles: present lda\.w REG_VMDATAL\S*\n((?!jmp|@)[\s\S])*?tax\n\tlda \d+,s\n\tsep #\$20\n\tsta\.l \$000000,x
in load_tiles: present lda\.w REG_VMDATAH\S*\n((?!jmp|@)[\s\S])*?tax\n\tlda \d+,s\n\tsep #\$20\n\tsta\.l \$000000,x
# The palette's high byte is color >> 8.
in load_palette: present lda \d+,s\n\txba\n\tand\.w #\$00FF
# state * 3 = (state << 1) + state.
in get_tile_for_state: present and\.w #\$00FF\n\tsta\.b tcc__r9\n\tasl a\n\tclc\n\tadc\.b tcc__r9
